package fail

// Package fail is a library whose tests, in fail_test.tck, fail in every
// way a test can, but for exit, which ends the run (see ../exits): errorf,
// which lets the test go on, fatalf, which stops it, an error a ?
// returns, reported at the ?, an error returned plainly, reported at
// the test's declaration, and a buffer the test allocated and did not
// free, also reported there. Tests that pass run between them, so each
// failure is seen to be the test's own. tack test exits 1. What the tests
// call is in fail_test.tck too, as nothing else calls it.

// Version is a declaration for the package to have beside its tests.
pub func Version() int64 {
    return 1
}
